# ============================================================
# AquaHub - Raw data
# Original datasets must not be versioned in Git
# ============================================================

data/raw/

# ============================================================
# AquaHub - Processed data
# Generated datasets can be reproduced from the pipeline, EXCEPT
# data/processed/pilot/: that's the small GeoJSON/JSON output the
# interactive platform's API (api/main.py) serves directly from disk.
# It must be committed, otherwise a stateless deploy (e.g. Vercel) has
# no data to serve and every endpoint 404s with a "run the build
# script locally" hint - see docs/03, Section 10.
#
# EXCEPT the exception: data/processed/pilot/indices/*.tif (the
# bioclimatic-index rasters) are NOT committed either (Sept 2026) -
# they got too big (~136MB) to bundle into the deployed Vercel
# function alongside its Python deps without hitting the platform's
# 225MB Lambda size limit. They live in Vercel Blob storage instead
# (api/main.py fetches + caches them on demand - see
# INDEX_BLOB_BASE_URL) and are only regenerated/re-uploaded locally
# when scripts/build_index_pilot_data.py's output changes. The small
# *_stats.json sidecars and indices_catalog.json stay committed as
# before - only the big rasters moved out.
# ============================================================

data/processed/*
!data/processed/pilot/
data/processed/pilot/indices/*.tif

# ============================================================
# AquaHub - Generated outputs
# ============================================================

outputs/figures/
outputs/tables/

